course: dictionary
lesson: 718
title: A barn is more than a shed
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A barn is a big farm building for animals, hay, crops or tools. The dictionary gives the short meaning, but the sentences around the word add clues. Hay is cut, dried and baled, and then it is kept safe, so a barn is a place where things are stored.
explain: Words next to barn change its meaning. «Barn owl» names a kind of bird that often lives in barns. «Barn dance» names a party with country dancing, so the word dance tells you the main idea. Look at the words before and after a word to find its meaning.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Put «farm building» in place of barn in «The hay was kept safe in the farm building» and it still makes sense. If it does, you have probably got the right meaning.
fact: A barn is a big farm building for animals, hay, crops or tools.
fact: «Barn owls» often live in barns, and a family of barn owls can eat over a thousand mice and voles in a year.
fact: «Barn dance» is a party with country dancing.
fact: Wet hay goes mouldy, and damp hay packed in a barn can get hot and even catch fire.
fact: There are about 250 kinds of owl, and owls live on every continent except Antarctica.
exercise: «A family of barn owls can eat over a thousand mice and voles in a year.» What is a barn owl? | *A bird that often lives in barns | A farm tool for cutting hay | A big farm animal | A dance at a country party
exercise: «Wet hay goes mouldy, and damp hay packed in a barn can get hot and even catch fire.» Why is damp hay a danger in a barn? | It turns into a dance floor | *It can get hot and even catch fire | It keeps the barn owls warm | It makes the barn grow bigger
exercise: Nadia says «barn dance» must mean a dance inside a barn. What does barn dance mean? | A dance on the roof of a barn | *A party with country dancing | A dance done only by owls | A dance for cows
test: «The rich fool built bigger barns to store his wealth, but died that night.» What does store mean here? | *Keep safe for later | Throw away | Paint in bright colours | Sell to strangers
test: Ella says, «I couldn't hit a barn door with a ball.» What does she mean? | She is very good at painting doors | She loves dancing at barns | *She is very bad at aiming | She hit the barn door every time
exam: Which sentence about a barn is correct? | A barn is a type of owl | A barn is a loud country song | *A barn is a big farm building for animals, hay, crops or tools | A barn is a small pond where fish live
